    "taxonId": 50837,
    "summary": "Mostly summer annuals, rarely perennials, native to the Americas and found mainly in desert or semi-desert habitats. Most form a basal rosette of divided leaves and produce five-lobed blue, white, pink or yellow flowers.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p3"],
