    "taxonId": 51122,
    "summary": "Aquatic annual or perennial herbs with a worldwide natural distribution. Most leaves float, while the solitary flowers may float or rise above the water and open during either the day or night.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "Despite general toxicity, some species’ boiled rhizomes and tubers are eaten, sometimes as famine food; seeds and some tubers are exceptions to the stated poison.",
