    "taxonId": 51224,
    "summary": "Cacti native to the coastal mountains of southeastern Brazil, where they grow on trees or rocks in shady, humid habitats. They are leafless, with green linked stems that are usually flattened into leaf-like pads, and flowers emerge from the joints and tips.",
